maintext_8139=The chariot can be said to be the most powerful chess piece in Chinese chess, because
ZZAnswerText1_8139=The name sounds very powerful
ZZAnswerText2_8139=Each move can go straight, retreat, and move horizontally, without limitation of steps
maintext_8140=In Chinese chess, can the pawn (soldier) move forward and backward after crossing the border?
ZZAnswerText1_8140=Can only move forward, cannot move backward
ZZAnswerText2_8140=Cannot move forward, can only move backward
maintext_8141=How many types of pawns are there in Chinese chess?
ZZAnswerText1_8141=6
ZZAnswerText2_8141=7
maintext_8142=What was Chinese chess called in ancient times?
ZZAnswerText1_8142=Elephant game
ZZAnswerText2_8142=Middle chess
maintext_8143=Where did Chinese chess originate?
ZZAnswerText1_8143=England
ZZAnswerText2_8143=Shanxi
maintext_8144=How many intersections are there on a Chinese chess board in total?
ZZAnswerText1_8144=90 intersections
ZZAnswerText2_8144=88 intersections
maintext_8145=What is it called when there are no straight lines drawn on the chess board?
ZZAnswerText1_8145=Nine Palace Grid
ZZAnswerText2_8145=River Boundary
maintext_8146=In official matches, does the red side move first or the black side?
ZZAnswerText1_8146=The black side
ZZAnswerText2_8146=Red Party
